{"id":"6e07bcf5346ff9ca","group":"58","path":"58/batch11/58-thm-filter-completeness.md","title":"Filter Completeness","display":"thm-filter-completeness — Filter Completeness","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-filter-completeness","aliases":["58-thm-filter-completeness","58-lem-filter-completeness"],"display":"thm-filter-completeness — Filter Completeness","depends_on":["[[../batch15/58-df-filter.md]]","[[58-df-cardinal]]","[[../batch09/58-df-powerset.md]]","[[../batch05/58-df-zfc-kappa-complete-filter.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-filter-completeness"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-filter-completeness</span><span>58-lem-filter-completeness</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-filter-completeness — Filter Completeness"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"1331244a5201bb99\" href=\"?note=1331244a5201bb99\" title=\"../batch15/58-df-filter.md\">../batch15/58-df-filter.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"5fb1c2241d1943d1\" href=\"?note=5fb1c2241d1943d1\" title=\"58-df-cardinal\">58-df-cardinal</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"2b6b1d9eb78a2714\" href=\"?note=2b6b1d9eb78a2714\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-powerset.md\">../batch09/58-df-powerset.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"56914510091eed27\" href=\"?note=56914510091eed27\" title=\"../batch05/58-df-zfc-kappa-complete-filter.md\">../batch05/58-df-zfc-kappa-complete-filter.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F\\subseteq\\mathcal P(X)\">\\(F\\subseteq\\mathcal P(X)\\)</span> (proper filter, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"1331244a5201bb99\" href=\"?note=1331244a5201bb99\" title=\"../batch15/58-df-filter.md\">../batch15/58-df-filter.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span> (cardinal, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"5fb1c2241d1943d1\" href=\"?note=5fb1c2241d1943d1\" title=\"58-df-cardinal\">58-df-cardinal</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Filter}_S,\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S,\\mathrm{KappaCompleteFilter}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Filter}_S,\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S,\\mathrm{KappaCompleteFilter}_S\\)</span> (predicates)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}filter-completeness} \\vdash \\mathrm{Filter}_S\\!\\left(F,\\mathcal P(X),\\{\\langle A,B\\rangle\\in\\mathcal P(X)^2:A\\subseteq B\\}\\right)\\land\\varnothing\\notin F\\to\\Bigl(\\mathrm{KappaCompleteFilter}_S(F,X,\\kappa)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\kappa\\neq0\\land\\forall\\mathcal A\\subseteq F\\;\\bigl(\\mathcal A\\neq\\varnothing\\land|\\mathcal A|&lt;\\kappa\\to\\bigcap\\mathcal A\\in F\\bigr)\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}filter-completeness} \\vdash \\mathrm{Filter}_S\\!\\left(F,\\mathcal P(X),\\{\\langle A,B\\rangle\\in\\mathcal P(X)^2:A\\subseteq B\\}\\right)\\land\\varnothing\\notin F\\to\\Bigl(\\mathrm{KappaCompleteFilter}_S(F,X,\\kappa)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\kappa\\neq0\\land\\forall\\mathcal A\\subseteq F\\;\\bigl(\\mathcal A\\neq\\varnothing\\land|\\mathcal A|&lt;\\kappa\\to\\bigcap\\mathcal A\\in F\\bigr)\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span>-completeness means closure under intersections of nonempty families of fewer than <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span> members; the empty-family case is represented separately by <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X\\in F\">\\(X\\in F\\)</span> in the proper-filter axioms.</li>\n<li>This formulation also covers set-complete filters, for which no least failing family exists.</li>\n<li>The nonzero-cardinal clause is required: for <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa=0\">\\(\\kappa=0\\)</span> the family-closure condition is vacuous, whereas the upstream <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span>-complete-filter predicate is false.</li>\n<li><code>58-lem-filter-completeness</code> is merged here; it asserted the same minimum-cardinal characterization.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch15/58-df-filter.md","status":"resolved","id":"1331244a5201bb99","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch15/58-df-filter.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-cardinal","status":"resolved","id":"5fb1c2241d1943d1","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-cardinal]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch09/58-df-powerset.md","status":"resolved","id":"2b6b1d9eb78a2714","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch09/58-df-powerset.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch05/58-df-zfc-kappa-complete-filter.md","status":"resolved","id":"56914510091eed27","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch05/58-df-zfc-kappa-complete-filter.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch15/58-df-filter.md","status":"resolved","id":"1331244a5201bb99","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]"